{"_id":"68a7360e8ec3d8323af12ebb","nodeId":"dSBYTGGkol3MAXyg7G7_J","roadmapSlug":"cloudflare","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:54.330Z","description":"# Node.js and NPM\n\nNode.js is an open source, cross-platform runtime environment and library that is used for running web applications outside the clientΓÇÖs browser. It is used for server-side programming, and primarily deployed for non-blocking, event-driven servers, such as traditional web sites and back-end API services, but was originally designed with real-time, push-based architectures in mind. Every browser has its own version of a JS engine, and node.js is built on Google ChromeΓÇÖs V8 JavaScript engine.\n\nnpm (Node Package Manager) is the standard package manager for Node.js. It is two things: first and foremost, it is an online repository for the publishing of open-source Node.js projects; second, it is a command-line utility for interacting with said repository that aids in package installation, version management, and dependency management.","resources":[{"type":"roadmap","title":"Visit Dedicated Node.js Roadmap","url":"https://roadmap.sh/nodejs","_id":"6a7f4a1bcb44947debcf3a0f"},{"type":"official","title":"Node.js Documentation","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/","_id":"6a7f4a1bcb44947debcf3a10"},{"type":"official","title":"NPM","url":"https://www.docs.npmjs.com/","_id":"6a7f4a1bcb44947debcf3a11"},{"type":"official","title":"An Introduction to NPM","url":"https://nodejs.org/en/learn/getting-started/an-introduction-to-the-npm-package-manager","_id":"6a7f4a1bcb44947debcf3a12"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:02:19.192Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a2aca8ed5b55a91aab11124","title":"JavaScript Foundations","slug":"javascript-foundations","description":"The JavaScript you need before Node.js, frontend frameworks, APIs, and CLI apps.","lessonIds":["6a27367ad5b55a91aab0e0cc","6a273f65d5b55a91aab0e124","6a27f0dad5b55a91aab0e2a9","6a27ff2ed5b55a91aab0e378","6a280307d5b55a91aab0e3df","6a281cbfd5b55a91aab0e47b","6a2889f2d5b55a